@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `br-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `br-lindb-conflict-of-laws`

-- Tests for br-lindb-conflict-of-laws.l4 (arts. 7 to 19). Every expected value was worked out from the text before the file was run.
-- Countries are made-up inputs ("Argentina", "Chile", ...) except "Brazil", which the text itself names.

§ `Art. 7 caput: the law of the domicile`

#ASSERT `the country whose law governs personality, name, capacity and family rights, for a person domiciled in` "Japan" EQUALS "Japan"

§ `Art. 7 par. 1: a marriage celebrated in Brazil`

#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the diriment impediments and the formalities of celebration of a marriage celebrated in` "Brazil" EQUALS "Brazil"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the country whose law governs the diriment impediments and the formalities of celebration of a marriage celebrated in` "Chile" BECAUSE "art. 7 par. 1 speaks only of a marriage celebrated in Brazil and says nothing of one celebrated elsewhere"

§ `Art. 7 par. 2: foreigners marrying before their own diplomatic or consular authority`

#ASSERT `art. 7 par. 2 allows the marriage of foreigners before the diplomatic or consular authority of` "Argentina" `and` "Argentina" `,` "Argentina"
-- the authority is not that of the country of both
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 2 allows the marriage of foreigners before the diplomatic or consular authority of` "Argentina" `and` "Argentina" `,` "Chile"
-- the spouses have different countries, so there is no "pais de ambos os nubentes"
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 2 allows the marriage of foreigners before the diplomatic or consular authority of` "Argentina" `and` "Chile" `,` "Argentina"
-- two Brazilians are not foreigners
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 2 allows the marriage of foreigners before the diplomatic or consular authority of` "Brazil" `and` "Brazil" `,` "Brazil"

§ `Art. 7 par. 3: invalidity of a marriage, spouses with different domiciles`

#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the invalidity of a marriage, for spouses domiciled in` "Chile" `and` "Peru" `with a first conjugal domicile in` "Bolivia" EQUALS "Bolivia"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the country whose law governs the invalidity of a marriage, for spouses domiciled in` "Chile" `and` "Chile" `with a first conjugal domicile in` "Bolivia" BECAUSE "art. 7 par. 3 speaks only of spouses whose domiciles differ and says nothing of the invalidity of a marriage between spouses with the same domicile"

§ `Art. 7 par. 4: the regime of property`

-- same domicile: that country's law
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the regime of property, for spouses domiciled in` "Chile" `and` "Chile" `with a first conjugal domicile in` "Bolivia" EQUALS "Chile"
-- different domiciles: the first conjugal domicile
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the regime of property, for spouses domiciled in` "Chile" `and` "Peru" `with a first conjugal domicile in` "Bolivia" EQUALS "Bolivia"

§ `Art. 7 par. 5: the naturalised spouse and partial community of property`

#ASSERT `art. 7 par. 5 allows a request that the adoption of the regime of partial community of property be noted` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 5 allows a request that the adoption of the regime of partial community of property be noted` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 5 allows a request that the adoption of the regime of partial community of property be noted` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 5 allows a request that the adoption of the regime of partial community of property be noted` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 5 allows a request that the adoption of the regime of partial community of property be noted` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Art. 7 par. 6: a foreign divorce`

-- a judgment of 10 March 2025 and no judicial separation: the year ends on 10 March 2026
-- before the anniversary: not recognised; after: recognised; on the day itself the text does not say
#ASSERT NOT `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2025 3 10) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2026 3 9) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "art. 7 par. 6 says recognition comes only after 1 year from the date of the judgment, and the text does not say whether the anniversary day is itself after that year"
#ASSERT `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2026 3 11) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2030 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE FALSE
-- a preceding judicial separation for an equal term: immediate effect, from the day of the judgment
#ASSERT `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2025 3 10) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2025 3 11) (YMD 2025 3 10) TRUE TRUE
-- the separation does not matter where neither spouse is Brazilian: the sentence is about divorces of Brazilians
#ASSERT REFUSED `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2025 3 11) (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "art. 7 par. 6 speaks only of a foreign divorce where one or both spouses are Brazilian"
-- a divorce of two foreigners is not within par. 6
#ASSERT REFUSED `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2030 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 10) FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "art. 7 par. 6 speaks only of a foreign divorce where one or both spouses are Brazilian"
-- a judgment of 29 February 2024: "one year" has no agreed anniversary, so the text gives no answer without a separation
#ASSERT REFUSED `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2025 2 28) (YMD 2024 2 29) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2030 1 1) (YMD 2024 2 29) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "the month reached has no day with the number of the starting day, and the text does not say what to do"
#ASSERT `the waiting rule of art. 7 par. 6 is met on` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 29) TRUE TRUE

-- second sentence: re-examination on request by the Superior Tribunal de Justica
#ASSERT `art. 7 par. 6 allows the Superior Tribunal de Justica to re-examine the decision` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 6 allows the Superior Tribunal de Justica to re-examine the decision` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 7 par. 6 allows the Superior Tribunal de Justica to re-examine the decision` TRUE FALSE

§ `Art. 7 par. 7: the domicile of the head of the family and of the guardian`

-- a person's situation is built from seven answers, in this order:
--   own domicile, other spouse of the head, unemancipated child of the head, head's domicile, incapable under a guardian, guardian's domicile, abandonment
GIVEN own IS A STRING
      spouse IS A BOOLEAN
      child IS A BOOLEAN
      head IS A STRING
      incapable IS A BOOLEAN
      guardian IS A STRING
      abandoned IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person's situation for art. 7 par. 7`
`a person who has` own spouse child head incapable guardian abandoned MEANS
    `A person's situation for art. 7 par. 7` WITH
        `the domicile the person has of their own` IS own
      , `the person is the other spouse of the head of the family` IS spouse
      , `the person is an unemancipated child of the head of the family` IS child
      , `the domicile of the head of the family` IS head
      , `the person is an incapable person under a guardian or curator` IS incapable
      , `the domicile of the guardian or curator` IS guardian
      , `there is a case of abandonment` IS abandoned

-- the other spouse takes the head's domicile
#ASSERT `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" TRUE FALSE "Chile" FALSE "Bolivia" FALSE) EQUALS "Chile"
-- an unemancipated child takes the head's domicile
#ASSERT `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" FALSE TRUE "Chile" FALSE "Bolivia" FALSE) EQUALS "Chile"
-- an incapable person under a guardian takes the guardian's
#ASSERT `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" FALSE FALSE "Chile" TRUE "Bolivia" FALSE) EQUALS "Bolivia"
-- none of these: the person's own
#ASSERT `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" FALSE FALSE "Chile" FALSE "Bolivia" FALSE) EQUALS "Peru"
-- "Salvo o caso de abandono": abandonment leaves the person with their own domicile, whichever extension would have applied
#ASSERT `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" TRUE FALSE "Chile" FALSE "Bolivia" TRUE) EQUALS "Peru"
#ASSERT `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" FALSE FALSE "Chile" TRUE "Bolivia" TRUE) EQUALS "Peru"
-- within both extensions with different domiciles: the text does not say which prevails
#ASSERT REFUSED `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" FALSE TRUE "Chile" TRUE "Bolivia" FALSE) BECAUSE "art. 7 par. 7 extends the domicile of the head of the family and that of the guardian or curator, and the text does not say which prevails for a person within both"
-- within both with the same domicile: both extensions agree
#ASSERT `the domicile of the person under art. 7 par. 7` (`a person who has` "Peru" FALSE TRUE "Chile" TRUE "Chile" FALSE) EQUALS "Chile"

§ `Art. 7 par. 8: a person with no domicile`

#ASSERT `the domicile of a person who has none, with a residence` NOTHING `and found in` "Chile" EQUALS "Chile"
#ASSERT `the domicile of a person who has none, with a residence` (JUST "Chile") `and found in` "Chile" EQUALS "Chile"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the domicile of a person who has none, with a residence` (JUST "Peru") `and found in` "Chile" BECAUSE "art. 7 par. 8 says residence or the place where the person is found, and the text does not say which prevails for a person who has a residence elsewhere"

§ `Art. 8: property`

#ASSERT `the country whose law governs property` `property in general` `situated in` "Argentina" `owned by one domiciled in` "Portugal" `possessed by one domiciled in` "Chile" EQUALS "Argentina"
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs property` `a movable the owner brings or means to carry to other places` `situated in` "Argentina" `owned by one domiciled in` "Portugal" `possessed by one domiciled in` "Chile" EQUALS "Portugal"
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs property` `a thing in pledge` `situated in` "Argentina" `owned by one domiciled in` "Portugal" `possessed by one domiciled in` "Chile" EQUALS "Chile"

§ `Art. 9: obligations`

#ASSERT `the country whose law qualifies and governs an obligation constituted in` "Uruguay" EQUALS "Uruguay"
#ASSERT `the country in which an obligation resulting from a contract is deemed constituted, the proponent residing in` "Peru" EQUALS "Peru"
#ASSERT `the essential form of Brazilian law is observed under art. 9 par. 1` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the essential form of Brazilian law is observed under art. 9 par. 1` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the essential form of Brazilian law is observed under art. 9 par. 1` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `art. 9 par. 1 admits a peculiarity of the foreign law` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 9 par. 1 admits a peculiarity of the foreign law` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 9 par. 1 admits a peculiarity of the foreign law` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 9 par. 1 admits a peculiarity of the foreign law` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `Art. 10: succession`

-- a foreigner domiciled in Italy with assets in Brazil, a Brazilian child benefits
-- the personal law is not more favourable to the child: Brazilian law (par. 1)
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs a succession` "Italy" TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Brazil"
-- the personal law is more favourable: the caput's law of the domicile
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs a succession` "Italy" TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Italy"
-- no Brazilian benefits: the domicile
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs a succession` "Italy" TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Italy"
-- not a foreigner with assets in Brazil: the domicile
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs a succession` "Italy" FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Italy"
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the capacity to succeed, the heir or legatee being domiciled in` "Spain" EQUALS "Spain"

§ `Art. 11: organisations and foreign governments`

#ASSERT `the country whose law governs an organisation constituted in` "Ireland" EQUALS "Ireland"
#ASSERT `art. 11 par. 1 forbids a branch, agency or establishment in Brazil` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 11 par. 1 forbids a branch, agency or establishment in Brazil` TRUE
#ASSERT `the country whose law an organisation with a branch in Brazil is subject to` EQUALS "Brazil"
-- par. 2 alone: a foreign government and an immovable
#ASSERT `art. 11 par. 2 forbids the acquisition` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `art. 11 par. 2 forbids the acquisition` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 11 par. 2 forbids the acquisition` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 11 par. 2 forbids the acquisition` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- par. 3 alone
#ASSERT `art. 11 par. 3 allows the acquisition` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 11 par. 3 allows the acquisition` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 11 par. 3 allows the acquisition` FALSE TRUE
-- the two together: a foreign government, immovable, building needed for the seat: par. 3 (fork F-11)
#ASSERT `a foreign government or its organisation may acquire the property in Brazil` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- a foreign government, immovable, not for the seat: par. 2 forbids
#ASSERT NOT `a foreign government or its organisation may acquire the property in Brazil` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- an organisation of a foreign government is not within par. 3 even for a seat building
#ASSERT NOT `a foreign government or its organisation may acquire the property in Brazil` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- neither speaks: a foreign government acquiring something that is neither immovable nor susceptible to expropriation, not for a seat
#ASSERT REFUSED `a foreign government or its organisation may acquire the property in Brazil` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "neither par. 2 nor par. 3 of art. 11 speaks to this acquisition"
-- neither a government nor an organisation of one
#ASSERT REFUSED `a foreign government or its organisation may acquire the property in Brazil` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "neither par. 2 nor par. 3 of art. 11 speaks to this acquisition"

§ `Art. 12: the competence of the Brazilian judicial authority`

#ASSERT `the Brazilian judicial authority is competent on a ground listed in art. 12 caput` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the Brazilian judicial authority is competent on a ground listed in art. 12 caput` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the Brazilian judicial authority is competent on a ground listed in art. 12 caput` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Brazilian judicial authority is competent on a ground listed in art. 12 caput` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "art. 12 caput names two grounds of competence and the text does not say whether there are others"
#ASSERT `only the Brazilian judicial authority may hear the action, under art. 12 par. 1` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `only the Brazilian judicial authority may hear the action, under art. 12 par. 1` FALSE
#ASSERT `the Brazilian judicial authority carries out the letter rogatory under art. 12 par. 2` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Brazilian judicial authority carries out the letter rogatory under art. 12 par. 2` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Brazilian judicial authority carries out the letter rogatory under art. 12 par. 2` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the form of carrying out a letter rogatory` EQUALS "Brazil"
#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the object of the measures of a letter rogatory from` "Spain" EQUALS "Spain"

§ `Arts. 13 and 14: foreign facts and foreign law`

#ASSERT `the country whose law governs the burden and the means of proving a fact that occurred in` "Mexico" EQUALS "Mexico"
-- a means of proof the foreign place admits and Brazilian law does not know: not admitted
#ASSERT `a Brazilian court admits the means of proof of a fact that occurred abroad` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a Brazilian court admits the means of proof of a fact that occurred abroad` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a Brazilian court admits the means of proof of a fact that occurred abroad` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `art. 14 allows the judge to require of the party invoking it proof of the text and force of the foreign law` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 14 allows the judge to require of the party invoking it proof of the text and force of the foreign law` TRUE

§ `Art. 15: a foreign judgment executed in Brazil`

-- a judgment is built from seven answers, in this order:
--   competent judge, parties served, default legally verified, res judicata, formalities of the place, authorised translation, homologated
GIVEN competent IS A BOOLEAN
      served IS A BOOLEAN
      default IS A BOOLEAN
      final IS A BOOLEAN
      formalities IS A BOOLEAN
      translated IS A BOOLEAN
      homologated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A foreign judgment, for art. 15`
`a foreign judgment where` competent served default final formalities translated homologated MEANS
    `A foreign judgment, for art. 15` WITH
        `it was given by a competent judge` IS competent
      , `the parties were served` IS served
      , `default was legally verified` IS default
      , `it has become res judicata` IS final
      , `it has the formalities necessary for execution in the place where it was given` IS formalities
      , `it is translated by an authorised interpreter` IS translated
      , `it has been homologated by the Supremo Tribunal Federal` IS homologated

#ASSERT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (b) is met by service or by a default legally verified
#ASSERT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- each other requirement missing
#ASSERT NOT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the foreign judgment meets the requirements of art. 15` (`a foreign judgment where` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Arts. 16 and 17: renvoi, and what offends`

#ASSERT NOT `a foreign law's remission to another law is considered`
#ASSERT `art. 17 denies the foreign law, act, judgment or declaration of will efficacy in Brazil` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `art. 17 denies the foreign law, act, judgment or declaration of will efficacy in Brazil` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `art. 17 denies the foreign law, act, judgment or declaration of will efficacy in Brazil` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `art. 17 denies the foreign law, act, judgment or declaration of will efficacy in Brazil` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 17 denies the foreign law, act, judgment or declaration of will efficacy in Brazil` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Art. 18: the consular authorities`

#ASSERT `the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` `the celebration of a marriage` `when` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` `another act of civil registry` `when` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` `a notarial act` `when` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` `the registration of the birth of a child of a Brazilian born in the country where the consulate sits` `when` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` `the registration of the death of a child of a Brazilian born in the country where the consulate sits` `when` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` `the celebration of a marriage` `when` FALSE BECAUSE "art. 18 caput speaks only of acts concerning Brazilians and says nothing of the consular authority's competence for others"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Brazilian consular authority is competent under art. 18 caput for` `a notarial act` `when` FALSE BECAUSE "art. 18 caput speaks only of acts concerning Brazilians and says nothing of the consular authority's competence for others"

-- par. 1: all seven conditions
#ASSERT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 18 par. 1 allows the consular authority to celebrate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- par. 2: a lawyer is indispensable, by subscribing the petition with both parties or with one whose spouse has their own lawyer
#ASSERT `the assistance of a lawyer required by art. 18 par. 2 is given` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the assistance of a lawyer required by art. 18 par. 2 is given` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the assistance of a lawyer required by art. 18 par. 2 is given` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the assistance of a lawyer required by art. 18 par. 2 is given` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the assistance of a lawyer required by art. 18 par. 2 is given` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the lawyer's signature on the public deed is required`

§ `Art. 19: validation of earlier consular acts, and the 90 days`

#ASSERT `art. 19 caput validates the act` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 19 caput validates the act` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 19 caput validates the act` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `art. 19 caput validates the act` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- the publication day of "this law" is an input; 10 March 2026 is made up. The 89th day after it is 7 June, the 90th is 8 June.
#ASSERT NOT `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 3 9) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 3 10) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 3 11) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE
#ASSERT `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE
#ASSERT `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 6 7) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 6 8) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE BECAUSE "the text does not say whether the day a period is counted from is itself counted"
#ASSERT NOT `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 6 9) (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE
-- the consular authorities had not refused: the paragraph does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `art. 19 sole paragraph allows the request to be renewed on` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE
